{
  "draft_response": "Hi there — thanks for reporting this. I’m sorry for the disruption to your production order processing.\n\nI can see you’re seeing “retries exhausted” for 118 events and that your webhook endpoint appears to have stopped receiving events from our system, even though you didn’t change anything on your side. We’ll need a bit more detail to confirm exactly which delivery attempts failed and whether a replay is available for those specific events.\n\nCould you please share the following?\n1) The webhook endpoint URL/environment you’re expecting events in (e.g., production vs. sandbox), and the account/store identifier(s) affected.\n2) The approximate time window when events stopped being delivered and when the retries became exhausted.\n3) The event types and/or identifiers shown for the 118 exhausted retries (a screenshot is fine).\n4) What your dashboard shows for those events—specifically any error messages and HTTP status codes (if available), or whether they show as “no delivery received.”\n5) Whether you’ve already attempted a replay (e.g., dashboard replay action/API call) and what happened.\n\nOnce we have this, we’ll escalate to our engineering team to review the delivery/retry history for those events and advise on the available replay options.",
  "tone": "escalation",
  "promised_actions": [
    "Escalate the ticket to our engineering team for review of the webhook delivery/retry history for the affected events",
    "Advise on the available replay options once we have the requested details"
  ],
  "safety_notes": [
    "We cannot confirm replay availability or success without reviewing the specific event identifiers/time window.",
    "We avoid promising delivery of missing events until engineering confirms what replay mechanisms are available and the root of the delivery interruption."
  ]
}
